# Store every text file with LF, in the repository and in the working copy.
#
# Two reasons this matters here rather than being the usual bikeshed:
#
#  * Git's Windows default rewrites text to CRLF on checkout, so without this the
#    .py files would arrive differently depending on who cloned them.
#  * prompts/*.txt are read byte-for-byte and sent to the model as its system
#    prompt. A CRLF checkout would not be the same document as the LF one, and
#    the difference would be invisible until a prompt mysteriously behaved
#    differently on someone else's machine.
#
# Python, JavaScript and JSON are all fine with LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.gguf binary
*.safetensors binary
